    <bpmn:process id="W_W3197" name="W3197. Lease Renewal, Escalation &amp; Rent Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Lease expiry approaching (12–18 months out); scheduled escalation; market-rent review clause
Frequency: Per lease event
Volume: ~205+ intercompany leases + ~200–600 third-party leases
Owner: Leasing Manager
Participants: Leasing Mgr, Property Mgr, Finance/Tax (links to VS-79/VS-72), Legal, Store Ops
Source: workflow W3197 — Lease Renewal, Escalation &amp; Rent Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3197_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3197_Lane1" name="Leasing Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3197_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3197_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3197_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3197_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3197_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3197_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3197_Start4" name="Lease expiry approaching (12–18 months out); scheduled escalation; market-rent review…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3197_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3197_Task5" name="Leasing Mgr/Finance analyze renewal economics: current vs market rent…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Leasing Mgr/Finance analyze renewal economics: current vs market rent (benchmark to W3207), tenant credit and performance, renewal vs reletting cost/benefit, capex requirements; for intercompany, refresh arm&#x27;s-length benchmark (links to VS-72); prepare renewal recommendation
Responsible (R): Leasing Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3197_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3197_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3197_Task6" name="Negotiate and execute renewal: rent and escalation terms, TI for renewal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Negotiate and execute renewal: rent and escalation terms, TI for renewal, term/options, updated clauses (insurance W3204, regulatory compliance); apply scheduled escalations automatically; Legal reviews and amends lease
Responsible (R): Leasing Mgr / Legal
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 4–12 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3197_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3197_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3197_Task7" name="Finance update lease accounting and billing (W3195): revised straight-line…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Finance update lease accounting and billing (W3195): revised straight-line schedule, new commencement/term, re-measurement under PFRS 16 if terms modified; update property master and portfolio analytics (W3208)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Lease Admin
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3197_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3197_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3197_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3197_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3197_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-134 (ensure property income &amp; LGU tax compliance (as owner).) | - operational: early engagement (12–18 months) and renewal incentives; operational: lease-admin calendar and automated billing
Owner: Leasing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
