    <bpmn:process id="W_W3200" name="W3200. Outlot, Pad &amp; Ground Lease Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Surplus land/outlot; ground-lease opportunity; pad development
Frequency: Per deal + ongoing
Volume: ~50–150 pad/outlot opportunities across portfolio
Owner: Leasing Manager
Participants: Leasing Mgr, Property Development Mgr (links to W3188), Legal, Finance, Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Source: workflow W3200 — Outlot, Pad &amp; Ground Lease Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3200_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3200_Lane1" name="Leasing Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3200_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3200_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3200_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3200_Lane2" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3200_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3200_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3200_Start4" name="Surplus land/outlot; ground-lease opportunity; pad development">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3200_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3200_Task5" name="Leasing/Property Dev identify pad/outlot opportunities: surplus land on owned…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Leasing/Property Dev identify pad/outlot opportunities: surplus land on owned sites, market demand (QSR, banks, fuel, pharmacies, logistics hubs), ground-lease vs out-right pad sale economics, BuildRight-store adjacency/traffic benefit; obtain investment approval
Responsible (R): Leasing Mgr / Property Dev Mgr
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 4–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3200_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3200_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3200_Task6" name="Legal/Leasing structure and execute: ground lease (long-term, tenant builds) vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Legal/Leasing structure and execute: ground lease (long-term, tenant builds) vs BuildRight-built pad for lease (W3188 TI), rent reset/review mechanisms, reversion at term, tenant build obligations and approvals, exclusivity/co-tenancy; account for lessor ground lease under PFRS 16
Responsible (R): Legal / Leasing Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 4–12 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3200_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3200_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3200_Task7" name="Ongoing management: pad-tenant billing (W3195), CAM, compliance monitoring…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ongoing management: pad-tenant billing (W3195), CAM, compliance monitoring (W3196), renewal/escalation (W3197); portfolio reporting on outlot yield and contribution to overall property NOI (W3201/W3208)
Responsible (R): Leasing Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3200_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3200_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3200_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3200_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3200_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-521 (ensure controlled execution — Landlord Leasing Operations &amp; Tenant Management (PA-97.2).) | - operational: maintenance covenants and reversion inspection; operational: use-clause/exclusivity protections
Owner: Leasing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
